From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fardjad Davari <public@fardjad.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 18:02:58 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat: add worker blueprints with runtime integration

X-Jcode-Patch-Intent: enable reusable worker blueprints with coordinator policy, generated tools, and bounded paginated output
X-Jcode-Patch-Kind: personal-feature
X-Jcode-Patch-Depends-On: none

Patch intent:
Add a worker blueprint system that lets a jcode user define reusable,
specialized subagent roles in Markdown. Each blueprint supplies durable
role instructions, model, effort, allowed-tools, communication-policy,
and timeout. At runtime, every valid blueprint generates a coordinator-
visible tool named swarm_<id> that spawns a blueprint-backed worker,
waits for completion, and returns a compact summary with paginated
follow-up reads. A coordinator-only tool policy (agents.coordinator)
restricts the coordinator's own tools without affecting internal roles
or spawned workers.

Why it exists:
Worker blueprints let a user specialize subagents without code changes.
A blueprint can pin a cheap model for routine work, restrict its tool
access, control its communication, and cap its runtime. The generated
tool returns a bounded summary (2000 chars) so the coordinator does not
burn tokens reading the worker's full output. A deterministic follow-up
read (no LLM) lets the coordinator page through more output in 2000-char
chunks when needed. The coordinator policy lets a user remove broad tools
like bash and generic swarm from the coordinator while retaining them for
authorized specialized workers and internal agents.

Upstream integration points:
- crates/jcode-config-types/src/lib.rs: CoordinatorConfig struct,
  swarm_timeout_minutes field, timeout_minutes on WorkerBlueprintOverride,
  coordinator and worker_blueprints fields on AgentsConfig.
- crates/jcode-base/src/config.rs: re-exports CoordinatorConfig.
- crates/jcode-base/src/worker_blueprint.rs: blueprint discovery, front-
  matter parsing, schema validation, override merging, diagnostics, and
  Display impl for WorkerBlueprintDiagnostic.
- crates/jcode-protocol/src/wire.rs: blueprint field on CommSpawn.
- crates/jcode-app-core/src/agent.rs: apply_coordinator_policy applied
  to root sessions in new_with_initial_ownership.
- crates/jcode-app-core/src/server/comm_session.rs: blueprint resolution,
  prompt composition, tool policy application, communication policy
  storage in spawn_swarm_agent.
- crates/jcode-app-core/src/server/client_comm_message.rs: communication
  policy enforcement in handle_comm_message.
- crates/jcode-app-core/src/server/state.rs: communication_policy field
  on SwarmMember.
- crates/jcode-app-core/src/tool/blueprint.rs: BlueprintTool implementing
  the Tool trait. Spawn mode: spawn, await, return compact summary with
  session ID. Follow-up mode: deterministic paginated read of stored
  output. Timeout resolved per-call > blueprint > config > default (20m).
- crates/jcode-app-core/src/tool/mod.rs: register_blueprint_tools in
  Registry::new.
- crates/jcode-app-core/src/tool/communicate.rs: blueprint field in
  CommunicateInput and spawn action.
- crates/jcode-app-core/src/tool/communicate/transport.rs: send_request
  and send_request_with_timeout made pub(crate) for blueprint tool reuse.

Update guidance:
Preserve the precedence chain for model (per-spawn > blueprint >
swarm_model > coordinator) and timeout (per-call > blueprint >
config > default 20m). Blueprint allowed-tools are always intersected
with the global tool policy. Coordinator policy only applies to root
sessions, never to spawned workers or internal roles. Communication-
policy: none blocks ordinary messages but not tool results. Generated
tools never overwrite existing tool names. All test SwarmMember and
WorkerBlueprintOverride constructions must include the new fields.

Validation:
cargo test -p jcode-app-core blueprint --lib
cargo test -p jcode-base worker_blueprint --lib
cargo test -p jcode-protocol --lib
cargo test -p jcode-config-types --lib
cargo check -p jcode-app-core
